# Prettier's HTML/Vue pre-parser misinterprets TypeScript generic syntax
# (e.g. `rawOf<EndpointOption>(item)`) inside `{{ }}` mustaches as opening
# HTML tags, causing spurious "Unexpected closing tag" parse errors.
#
# The templates render correctly at runtime (Vue's template compiler parses
# mustache contents as JS, not HTML), and the same `rawOf<T>(...)` expression
# is accepted by Prettier when used inside attribute bindings on the same
# file. Rewriting around this limitation would either lose template-side
# type safety or require structural changes that hurt readability.
#
# Re-evaluate when Prettier improves Vue template generic handling.
